      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS exceeds analyst expectations while revenues lag behind",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹11.56 (up from ₹9.13 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹82.9b (up 14% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹4.19b (up 27% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 5.1% (up from 4.6% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue missed analyst estimates by 1.1%. Earnings per share (EPS) exceeded analyst estimates by 4.5%. Revenue is forecast to grow 13% p.a. on average during the next 3 years, compared to a 13% growth forecast for the Chemicals industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has fallen by 15% per year but the company’s share price has only fallen by 1% per year, which means it has not declined as severely as earnings.",
